ntor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERADA, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A power system (403) for an electric vehicle comprises a rechargeable battery (400), a battery control device (401) for controlling the state of the battery (400), including the remaining charge of the battery, and a charger (402) for charging the rechargeable battery (400). The charger (402) includes discharge means (404) for refreshing the rechargeable battery (400) and discharge control means (405) for controlling the refreshing by the discharge means (404) based on a refreshing signal from the battery control device (401).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Système (403) d'alimentation en puissance pour un véhicule électrique, qui comporte une batterie rechargeable (400), un dispositif de commande (401) de batterie destiné à contrôler l'état de la batterie, y compris la charge restante, et un chargeur (402) destiné à charger ladite batterie (400) rechargeable. Le chargeur (402) comporte un moyen de décharge (404) permettant de régénérer la batterie (400) rechargeable et un moyen de commande (405) de décharge destiné à commander la régénération par le moyen de décharge (404) sur la base d'un signal de régénération produit par le dispositif de commande (401) de batterie.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including bu